// The scheduler that keeps panel email going when no admin page is open.
//
// Cloudflare Pages cannot run on a timer, so this one-file Worker does: every
// minute it asks the site to send whatever is due (POST /api/cron/tick). The
// queue, the pace and Stop all live on the site; this Worker only knocks.
//
// Deploy once, from the repo root (the organiser's terminal):
//   npx wrangler deploy --config cron/wrangler.jsonc
//   echo "<the admin password, or a CRON_SECRET set on the Pages project>" | npx wrangler secret put CRON_SECRET --config cron/wrangler.jsonc
// Check it is knocking: Admin -> Overview -> Campus panels shows "scheduler seen
// N s ago" while a send is running, and the Worker's own logs show each tick:
//   npx wrangler tail --config cron/wrangler.jsonc
{
  "$schema": "../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "bharatai-mail-cron",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-02-20",
  "triggers": { "crons": ["* * * * *"] },
  "vars": { "SITE": "https://bharataiinnovation.com" }
}
